  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Halve the leek (see Kitchen 101) lengthwise and thinly slice the pale stem, discarding any dark green stem. Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove. Coarsely chop the dill, discarding the stems. Drain and rinse the beans.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2835556/photos/large/prep_ingredients-34e934d5b59a92cc85a8f673525229ff.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Soften leek: Heat 1½ tbs olive oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the leek, stirring occasionally, for 8 mins or until softened. Add the garlic and cook, stirring, for 1 min or until fragrant.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2835557/photos/large/soften_leek-cc3deab75901573bd2b19d43cb627ab4.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Simmer sauce: Add the beans, tomatoes, half the salsa, half the dill and 1 tsp sugar to the pan and stir to combine. Season with salt and pepper and bring to a simmer. Make 2 indents in the mixture, then crack 2 eggs into the indents. Reduce the heat to low and cook, covered, for 8-10 mins until the eggs are cooked to your liking. Remove the pan from the heat.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2835558/photos/large/simmer_sauce-e0fb130ea9fbf6c0bd79de51a5769a17.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Prep yoghurt: Meanwhile, put the yoghurt and remaining salsa in a bowl, season well with salt and pepper and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2835559/photos/large/make_capsicum_yoghurt-f935a515c4fff85db2268381d7bd98a6.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Scatter the remaining dill over the beans and eggs. Top with the yoghurt mixture and put the pan in the centre of the table for everyone to help themselves. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2835560/photos/large/serve_up-6b55a8625ae33fb6c72e279bc3562b1c.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Kitchen 101: Prior to chopping, give the pale part of the leek a good rinse under running water to remove any hidden dirt.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2835561/photos/large/kitchen_101-a02342818b32a89fdb315984f0855826.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
